        "The transition toward electric mobility has accelerated significantly over the last decade. In 2015, electric vehicles—both battery-electric and plug-in hybrids—accounted for only a tiny fraction of global vehicle sales. This early phase was characterized by niche adoption, limited public charging infrastructure, and higher initial costs compared to internal combustion engines.",
